Sketch version: thread-and-knots-v2, 2026-09-30. One task, one division,
one correction. Not a general expression editor.

v2 fixes three things iohan found by testing, not by reading:
1. There was no drop zone for the second (correction) drag — .tiezone only
   existed before the first knot. Added a second tie zone next to the active
   knot once one commit exists.
2. Typing "3.5" and pressing Enter tied it anyway, because parseInt() ran
   before the integer check. Now validates the raw Number() value, so a
   fractional or non-numeric entry is rejected and the field is left as
   typed for the author to see and correct.
3. Accessibility: dropped role="img" from the outer <svg> (it was hiding
   the button-beads from some accessibility trees) in favour of role="group",
   and focus now moves to the first active share bead after a correction
   lands, instead of to <body>. Not claiming this closes the accessibility
   item — untested with an actual screen reader, exactly the caveat iohan
   raised.
-->
